WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.699 --> 00:00:05.688
- [Narrator] To the north and west

00:00:05.688 --> 00:00:09.699
of Ireland's County Donegal,
is windswept Toraigh Island,

00:00:09.699 --> 00:00:13.616
surrounded by the hungry
waves of the Atlantic.

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:18.128
Less than 200 people live here,

00:00:18.128 --> 00:00:20.869
including Ireland's last and only king,

00:00:20.869 --> 00:00:24.699
a tradition that goes back 1400 years.

00:00:24.699 --> 00:00:26.560
- My name is Patsy Dan Rodgers,

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:28.309
the King of Toraigh, as they say,

00:00:28.309 --> 00:00:31.809
and you're very welcome to Toraigh Island.

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:39.687
- [Narrator] As king of the island,

00:00:39.687 --> 00:00:42.527
Patsy's role is mostly symbolic.

00:00:42.527 --> 00:00:45.255
In the sixth century, a
visiting saint created the role

00:00:45.255 --> 00:00:48.876
in order to unify the islanders
in defense of pirates.

00:00:48.876 --> 00:00:53.567
But Patsy's very proud of
his island's rich heritage.

00:00:53.567 --> 00:00:55.975
- [Patsy] We have our own Ghaeilge language.

00:00:55.975 --> 00:00:58.795
Everyone speaks Ghaeilge on the island.

00:00:58.795 --> 00:01:02.212
We have a very strong culture, musicians.

00:01:04.474 --> 00:01:06.172
- [Narrator] Patsy's
duties as king are few,

00:01:06.172 --> 00:01:10.391
but he takes his role as island
ambassador very seriously.

00:01:10.391 --> 00:01:13.132
- People come from various
parts of the world,

00:01:13.132 --> 00:01:15.926
from a number of countries
to meet me and to see me

00:01:15.926 --> 00:01:19.126
on the island and to talk to me.

00:01:19.126 --> 00:01:22.875
When I accepted the
simple honor of the king,

00:01:22.875 --> 00:01:24.905
I thought it would never come to what

00:01:24.905 --> 00:01:26.488
it did come to now.

00:01:27.625 --> 00:01:29.542
It's quite serious now.

00:01:32.198 --> 00:01:34.324
- [Narrator] Of the
roughly 150 people who live

00:01:34.324 --> 00:01:38.406
on Toraigh Island, many
are over 65 years old,

00:01:38.406 --> 00:01:40.217
and the island struggles for tourism

00:01:40.217 --> 00:01:42.185
and help from the mainland.

00:01:42.185 --> 00:01:43.404
- I am almost 70.

00:01:43.404 --> 00:01:46.425
Many are over 70, and
the island is not going

00:01:46.425 --> 00:01:49.770
to really depend on that type of age,

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:51.770
as much as we'd like to.

00:01:53.036 --> 00:01:55.147
They would like to see now the population

00:01:55.147 --> 00:01:59.516
of the island growing and
also a few jobs to teenagers

00:01:59.516 --> 00:02:02.627
and the island to start swinging again.

00:02:02.627 --> 00:02:05.127
(Irish music)

00:02:09.035 --> 00:02:11.438
- [Narrator] Patsy may
be the only Irish king,

00:02:11.438 --> 00:02:15.547
but his hope is that he won't be the last.

00:02:15.547 --> 00:02:19.096
- (Patsy) When I am on my dying
bed, hopefully before that,

00:02:19.096 --> 00:02:22.856
somebody will come up and
offer to take the honor

00:02:22.856 --> 00:02:25.023
of the King of the Island.

